        "content": {
          "content_type": "text",
          "parts": [
            "Perfect. With **milk and butter**, this becomes a rich, classic **cheesy broccoli\u2013cauliflower casserole**. I recommend **leaving the blue cheese out** for the best balance.\n\n\ue200image_group\ue202{\"query\":[\"broccoli cauliflower cheese casserole\",\"cheddar parmesan vegetable casserole\",\"baked broccoli cauliflower cheese\"]}\ue201\n\n---\n\n## \ud83e\uddc0 Creamy Broccoli Cauliflower Casserole (Cheddar + Parmesan)\n\n### Ingredients\n- 3 to 4 cups broccoli florets  \n- 3 to 4 cups cauliflower florets  \n- 2 tablespoons butter  \n- 2 tablespoons milk (add more if needed)  \n- 1\u00bd to 2 cups shredded cheddar cheese  \n- \u00bd cup parmesan cheese  \n- 1 clove garlic, minced (or \u00bd teaspoon garlic powder)  \n- Salt and pepper to taste  \n- Crumble dressing for topping  \n\n---\n\n### Instructions\n1. **Preheat oven** to 375\u00b0F.\n2. **Parboil vegetables**  \n   Boil broccoli and cauliflower in salted water for 3 to 4 minutes until just tender. Drain very well.\n3. **Make it creamy**  \n   While veggies are hot, toss them with:\n   - Butter\n   - Milk\n   - Cheddar\n   - Parmesan\n   - Garlic\n   - Salt and pepper  \n   Stir until the butter melts and everything looks lightly coated and creamy. Add a splash more milk if it feels dry.\n4. **Transfer to baking dish**\n5. **Top with crumble dressing**  \n   Sprinkle evenly over the top.\n6. **Bake uncovered**  \n   25 to 30 minutes until bubbly and golden on top.\n7. **Optional broil**  \n   Broil 1 to 2 minutes at the end for extra crunch. Watch closely.\n\n---\n\n### Want to use the blue cheese?\nIf you really want it, add **1 to 2 tablespoons max**, mixed in. Any more will overpower the dish.\n\n---\n\nThis will come out **comforting, cheesy, and perfectly balanced**.  \nIf you want it creamier, sharper, or more crispy on top, tell me and I will adjust it exactly how you like."
          ]
