            "You can absolutely turn that into a great casserole. The only real question is whether you *want* the blue cheese flavor. It is strong, but it can work if used lightly.\n\nBelow are **two solid options**, so you can choose based on taste.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83e\uddc0 Option 1: Creamy Cheddar\u2013Parmesan Veggie Casserole (Safest Crowd-Pleaser)\n**Skip the blue cheese entirely.** This will be rich, cozy, and classic.\n\n\ue200image_group\ue202{\"query\":[\"broccoli cauliflower cheese casserole\",\"cheddar parmesan vegetable casserole\",\"baked broccoli cauliflower cheese\"]}\ue201\n\n### Ingredients (what you have)\n- Broccoli, chopped\n- Cauliflower, chopped\n- Shredded cheddar\n- Parmesan cheese\n- Crumble dressing\n- Garlic (minced or powdered)\n- Salt & pepper\n- Optional if you have it: butter, splash of milk or cream\n\n### How to make it\n1. **Preheat oven** to 375\u00b0F.\n2. **Parboil veggies**  \n   Boil broccoli and cauliflower in salted water for 3 to 4 minutes. Drain well.\n3. **Make it creamy**\n   - Toss veggies with:\n     - 1\u00bd to 2 cups shredded cheddar  \n     - \u00bd cup parmesan  \n     - Garlic to taste  \n     - Salt & pepper  \n     - Optional: 1 to 2 tablespoons butter and a splash of milk or cream for extra richness\n4. **Transfer to casserole dish**\n5. **Top with crumble dressing**  \n   Lightly sprinkle over the top for crunch.\n6. **Bake uncovered** 25 to 30 minutes until bubbly and golden.\n\n\u2714\ufe0f This version is comforting and universally liked.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83e\uddc0 Option 2: Cheddar\u2013Blue Cheese Casserole (If You Like Bold Flavor)\n**Keep the blue cheese but use it sparingly.**\n\n\ue200image_group\ue202{\"query\":[\"blue cheese broccoli casserole\",\"broccoli cauliflower blue cheese bake\",\"cheddar blue cheese vegetable casserole\"]}\ue201\n\n### How to adjust\n- Use **mostly cheddar**\n- Add **just 2\u20133 tablespoons of blue cheese**, crumbled\n- Mix the blue cheese *into* the casserole, not on top\n\nThis gives a subtle tang without overpowering the dish.\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f If you use more than that, the blue cheese will dominate.\n\n---\n\n## My honest recommendation\nIf you are feeding others or want maximum comfort food vibes \ud83d\udc49 **leave the blue cheese out**.  \nIf it is just for you and you love blue cheese \ud83d\udc49 **add a small amount**, not more.\n\nIf you want, tell me:\n- Do you have milk, cream, or sour cream?\n- Are you serving this as a main or a side?\n\nI can tighten this into a perfect, no-fail version for what you are making."
          ]
