    "f2486217-d4c4-4b21-a7c0-30af3eb4abfc": {
      "id": "f2486217-d4c4-4b21-a7c0-30af3eb4abfc",
      "message": {
        "author": {
          "name": null,
          "role": "assistant"
        },
        "content": {
          "content_type": "text",
          "parts": [
            "Add the **onion crisps at the very end** so they stay crunchy.\n\n### Do this:\n1. Bake the casserole **uncovered for about 20 minutes** first.\n2. **Pull it out**, sprinkle the onion crisps evenly on top.\n3. Return to the oven for **5 to 10 minutes**, just until the cheese is bubbling and the onions are golden.\n4. If you want extra crunch, you can broil **30 to 60 seconds**, watching closely so they do not burn.\n\n**Rule of thumb:**  \nIf they go on too early, they get soggy or burn. Late = perfect crunch.\n\nYou are doing this exactly right."
          ]
        },
